Software	Version	Description
Cell Ranger	v10.0.0	Cell Ranger is the official data analysis pipeline provided by 10X Genomics for single-cell RNA-seq data. It processes Illumina raw sequencing data (FASTQ) into gene expression matrices, including FASTQ demultiplexing, sequence alignment (STAR), Barcode/UMI correction, and gene expression quantification.
STARsolo	v2.7.11a	STARsolo is a built-in single-cell analysis module of the STAR aligner. It serves as an alternative to Cell Ranger for sequence alignment and gene expression quantification, offering faster performance and supporting multiple single-cell library preparation platforms (including 10X Chromium 3' and 5' assays).
Seurat	v5.0.0	Seurat is an R package dedicated to single-cell RNA-seq analysis. Its functionality covers data filtering, normalization, batch effect removal, cell clustering, differential gene expression analysis, and more. It is feature-rich and widely adopted in the single-cell sequencing community.
SingleR	v2.2.0	SingleR compares each cluster from cell clustering results against reference databases, scoring clusters based on the similarity of their gene expression profiles to known cell populations. The resulting score matrix enables automated cell type annotation for each cluster.
CellChat	v2.0.0	CellChat quantitatively infers and analyzes intercellular communication networks from single-cell data. It uses network analysis and pattern recognition methods to predict major signaling inputs and outputs of cells, and how these cells and signals coordinate biological functions.
clusterProfiler	v4.10.0	clusterProfiler is an R package for gene enrichment analysis using multiple methods, such as GO and KEGG, with built-in visualization capabilities for enrichment analysis results.
Monocle3	v1.3.7	Monocle3 is an R package for pseudotime analysis. Based on differential gene expression across cell populations, it infers cell lineage development, constructs cell trajectory along a virtual time axis, and recapitulates the dynamic process of cell state transitions over time.
